WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
Draw a histogram of adult heights.

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.670
Then test marks.

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.720
Then the masses of bags
filled by a machine.

4
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.580
Three different things.

5
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.340
Yet each time, a bell-shaped
curve fits the bars.

6
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:17.200
One is in centimetres, one
in marks, one in grams.

7
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.910
Why does the same shape keep turning up?

8
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.240
Is it the units?

9
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.290
Does nature always make symmetric data?

10
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.550
In this mission, you'll meet
the normal distribution,

11
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.130
a continuous model fixed
by a mean and a spread.

12
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.460
You'll find probabilities
as areas under the curve.

13
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.040
And you'll standardise
to the standard normal,

14
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.040
then work backwards to a mean or a spread.

15
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: explain why such different
measurements share the same bell shape.
